{
  "id": "correspondence-bias",
  "term": "correspondence bias",
  "definition": "Correspondence bias is the tendency to explain another person’s behavior or performance as mainly reflecting their personal qualities, while giving too little weight to the situation or environment that helped shape the outcome. This can lead people to treat easier circumstances and higher apparent performance as signs of greater ability than they really are.",
